# Copy to .env.local for local development, and add the same two variables in
# Vercel under Settings -> Environment Variables.
#
# Both are compiled into the public JavaScript bundle, which is correct for
# these two and only these two. The anon key is an identity, not a
# permission -- Row Level Security decides what it may do.
#
# NEVER add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here or anywhere with a VITE_ prefix.
# service_role bypasses every RLS policy, so publishing it in the bundle
# hands your database to anyone who opens DevTools.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Note: as of v2.1 these are optional. src/lib/supabaseClient.js carries
# compiled-in production defaults, so a build without them still works.
# Set them to point a build at a different Supabase project.
